{"id":"mahabharata-9-061","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":61,"title":"एकषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 61 · The Pandavas celebrate and Krishna leaves","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas blow their conches in joy and go to the Kaurava camp, and Krishna speaks of how the war was won by his strategies. He leaves for Dwaraka after speaking with the Pandavas.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರು ಹರ್ಷದಿಂದ ಶಂಖ ಊದಿ ಕೌರವ ಶಿಬಿರಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ತನ್ನ ಉಪಾಯಗಳಿಂದ ಯುದ್ಧ ಗೆದ್ದುದನ್ನು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪಾಂಡವರೊಡನೆ ಮಾತನಾಡಿ ದ್ವಾರಕೆಗೆ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डव हर्ष से शंख बजाकर कौरव शिविर में जाते हैं, और कृष्ण अपने उपायों से युद्ध जीतने की बात कहते हैं। पाण्डवों से बात कर वे द्वारका को प्रस्थान करते हैं।","te":"పాండవులు సంతోషంతో శంఖాలు ఊది కౌరవ శిబిరానికి వెళతారు; తన ఉపాయాలతో యుద్ధం గెలిచిన తీరును కృష్ణుడు చెబుతాడు. పాండవులతో మాట్లాడి ద్వారకకు బయలుదేరతాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர் மகிழ்ந்து சங்கு முழங்கிக் கௌரவப் பாசறைக்குச் செல்ல, தன் உபாயங்களால் போர் வெல்லப்பட்டதைக் கண்ணன் கூறுகிறார். பாண்டவருடன் பேசி துவாரகைக்குப் புறப்படுகிறார்.","ml":"സന്തോഷത്തോടെ പാണ്ഡവർ ശംഖു മുഴക്കി കൗരവപാളയത്തിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു; തന്റെ തന്ത്രങ്ങളാലാണ് യുദ്ധം ജയിച്ചതെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ പറയുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവരോട് സംസാരിച്ച ശേഷം അദ്ദേഹം ദ്വാരകയിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.61; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"गदायुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Gadayuddha Parva (The mace fight)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्ते प्रययुः सर्वे निवासाय महीक्षितः ।\nशङ्खान्प्रध्मापयन्तो वै हृष्टाः परिघबाहवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all those kings set off to find lodging, glad, blowing their conches, their arms like iron bars."}},{"n":2,"text":"पाण्डवान्गच्छतश्चापि शिबिरं नो विशां पते ।\nमहेष्वासोऽन्वगात्पश्चाद्युयुत्सुः सात्यकिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Pandavas went to the camp, O lord of men, the great archers Yuyutsu and Satyaki followed behind."}},{"n":3,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः शिखण्डी च द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्वशः ।\nसर्वे चान्ये महेष्वासा ययुः स्वशिबिराण्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, Shikhandi, the sons of Draupadi, and all the other great archers went to their own camps."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततस्ते प्राविशन्पार्था हतत्विट्कं हतेश्वरम् ।\nदुर्योधनस्य शिबिरं रङ्गवद्विसृते जने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sons of Pritha entered Duryodhana's camp, now robbed of its splendour and of its lord, its people dispersed as from a deserted stage,"}},{"n":5,"text":"गतोत्सवं पुरमिव हृतनागमिव ह्रदम् ।\nस्त्रीवर्षवरभूयिष्ठं वृद्धामात्यैरधिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"like a city whose festival is over, or a lake whose elephant has been carried off, mostly filled with women and chamberlains and watched over by aged ministers."}},{"n":6,"text":"तत्रैतान्पर्युपातिष्ठन्दुर्योधनपुरःसराः ।\nकृताञ्जलिपुटा राजन्काषायमलिनाम्बराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, led by Duryodhana's people, with joined palms and wearing dirty saffron robes, they waited on them, O king."}},{"n":7,"text":"शिबिरं समनुप्राप्य कुरुराजस्य पाण्डवाः ।\nअवतेरुर्महाराज रथेभ्यो रथसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the camp of the Kuru king, the Pandavas, best of chariot-warriors, got down from their chariots, great king."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो गाण्डीवधन्वानमभ्यभाषत केशवः ।\nस्थितः प्रियहिते नित्यमतीव भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Keshava, always devoted to what is dear and good for him, spoke to the wielder of the Gandiva, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":9,"text":"अवरोपय गाण्डीवमक्षय्यौ च महेषुधी ।\nअथाहमवरोक्ष्यामि पश्चाद्भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Put down the Gandiva and the two great inexhaustible quivers; afterwards I shall get down, best of Bharatas.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"स्वयं चैवावरोह त्वमेतच्छ्रेयस्तवानघ ।\nतच्चाकरोत्तथा वीरः पाण्डुपुत्रो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And you yourself get down first; this is better for you, blameless one.\" The hero Arjuna, son of Pandu, did so."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ पश्चात्ततः कृष्णो रश्मीनुत्सृज्य वाजिनाम् ।\nअवारोहत मेधावी रथाद्गाण्डीवधन्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After that Krishna, the wise, let go of the horses' reins and got down from the chariot of the wielder of the Gandiva."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथावतीर्णे भूतानामीश्वरे सुमहात्मनि ।\nकपिरन्तर्दधे दिव्यो ध्वजो गाण्डीवधन्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that great-souled lord of beings had got down, the divine monkey on the banner of Gandiva's wielder vanished."}},{"n":13,"text":"स दग्धो द्रोणकर्णाभ्यां दिव्यैरस्त्रैर्महारथः ।\nअथ दीप्तोऽग्निना ह्याशु प्रजज्वाल महीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great chariot, burnt long before by the divine weapons of Drona and Karna, now suddenly blazed up with fire, O lord of the earth."}},{"n":14,"text":"सोपासङ्गः सरश्मिश्च साश्वः सयुगबन्धुरः ।\nभस्मीभूतोऽपतद्भूमौ रथो गाण्डीवधन्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The chariot of the wielder of the Gandiva, with its side-quivers, reins, horses and yoke-fittings, fell to the ground reduced to ashes."}},{"n":15,"text":"तं तथा भस्मभूतं तु दृष्ट्वा पाण्डुसुताः प्रभो ।\nअभवन्विस्मिता राजन्नर्जुनश्चेदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it turned to ashes, the sons of Pandu were amazed, O king, and Arjuna, with joined palms, bowing affectionately and honouring him, said this."}},{"n":16,"text":"कृताञ्जलिः सप्रणयं प्रणिपत्याभिवाद्य च ।\nगोविन्द कस्माद्भगवन्रथो दग्धोऽयमग्निना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Govinda, venerable one, why has this chariot been burnt by fire?\""}},{"n":17,"text":"किमेतन्महदाश्चर्यमभवद्यदुनन्दन ।\nतन्मे ब्रूहि महाबाहो श्रोतव्यं यदि मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What is this great marvel, delight of the Yadavas? Tell me, mighty-armed one, if you think I should hear it.\""}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अस्त्रैर्बहुविधैर्दग्धः पूर्वमेवायमर्जुन ।\nमदधिष्ठितत्वात्समरे न विशीर्णः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Arjuna, this was burnt long ago by many kinds of weapons, scorcher of enemies; because I was stationed on it, it did not fall to pieces in the battle.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"इदानीं तु विशीर्णोऽयं दग्धो ब्रह्मास्त्रतेजसा ।\nमया विमुक्तः कौन्तेय त्वय्यद्य कृतकर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But now it has crumbled, burnt by the power of the Brahma weapon, since I have left it, son of Kunti, now that your task is done.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"ईषदुत्स्मयमानश्च भगवान्केशवोऽरिहा ।\nपरिष्वज्य च राजानं युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a slight smile, the venerable Keshava, slayer of enemies, embraced King Yudhishthira and said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"दिष्ट्या जयसि कौन्तेय दिष्ट्या ते शत्रवो जिताः ।\nदिष्ट्या गाण्डीवधन्वा च भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By good fortune you have won, son of Kunti; by good fortune your enemies are beaten; by good fortune the wielder of the Gandiva and the Pandava Bhimasena are safe.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"त्वं चापि कुशली राजन्माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nमुक्ता वीरक्षयादस्मात्संग्रामान्निहतद्विषः ।\nक्षिप्रमुत्तरकालानि कुरु कार्याणि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You too are well, O king, and the two Pandava sons of Madri; you are freed from this slaughter of heroes, this battle, your enemies slain. Quickly do what must be done next, Bharata.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"उपयातमुपप्लव्यं सह गाण्डीवधन्वना ।\nआनीय मधुपर्कं मां यत्पुरा त्वमवोचथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When I came to Upaplavya with the wielder of the Gandiva, you said to me, after bringing the honey-offering,\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एष भ्राता सखा चैव तव कृष्ण धनंजयः ।\nरक्षितव्यो महाबाहो सर्वास्वापत्स्विति प्रभो ।\nतव चैवं ब्रुवाणस्य तथेत्येवाहमब्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Krishna, this Dhananjaya is your brother and friend, and he must be protected in every danger, mighty-armed lord.' When you said this to me, I answered 'So be it.'\""}},{"n":25,"text":"स सव्यसाची गुप्तस्ते विजयी च नरेश्वर ।\nभ्रातृभिः सह राजेन्द्र शूरः सत्यपराक्रमः ।\nमुक्तो वीरक्षयादस्मात्संग्रामाद्रोमहर्षणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King, that left-handed archer was protected by you, and he is victorious; that brave man of true valour, with his brothers, is freed from this hair-raising slaughter of heroes in battle.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु कृष्णेन धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nहृष्टरोमा महाराज प्रत्युवाच जनार्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed by Krishna, Yudhishthira, the king of dharma, his hair standing on end, answered Janardana."}},{"n":27,"text":"प्रमुक्तं द्रोणकर्णाभ्यां ब्रह्मास्त्रमरिमर्दन ।\nकस्त्वदन्यः सहेत्साक्षादपि वज्री पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who but you, scorcher of enemies, could withstand the Brahma weapon launched by Drona and Karna, even Indra the thunderbolt-wielder in person?\""}},{"n":28,"text":"भवतस्तु प्रसादेन संग्रामे बहवो जिताः ।\nमहारणगतः पार्थो यच्च नासीत्पराङ्मुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By your grace many were conquered in the battle, and Arjuna, in the great fight, never turned his back.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"तथैव च महाबाहो पर्यायैर्बहुभिर्मया ।\nकर्मणामनुसंतानं तेजसश्च गतिः शुभा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And likewise, mighty-armed one, with many turns of events there has been a continuing chain of deeds and a fortunate course of my power.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"उपप्लव्ये महर्षिर्मे कृष्णद्वैपायनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nयतो धर्मस्ततः कृष्णो यतः कृष्णस्ततो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At Upaplavya the great sage Krishna Dvaipayana told me: 'Where there is dharma, there is Krishna; where there is Krishna, there is victory.'\""}},{"n":31,"text":"इत्येवमुक्ते ते वीराः शिबिरं तव भारत ।\nप्रविश्य प्रत्यपद्यन्त कोशरत्नर्द्धिसंचयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When this had been said, those heroes entered your camp, Bharata, and took possession of the treasure, jewels and accumulated wealth."}},{"n":32,"text":"रजतं जातरूपं च मणीनथ च मौक्तिकान् ।\nभूषणान्यथ मुख्यानि कम्बलान्यजिनानि च ।\nदासीदासमसंख्येयं राज्योपकरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"They took silver, gold, gems and pearls, fine ornaments, blankets and deerskins, countless male and female slaves, and royal furnishings."}},{"n":33,"text":"ते प्राप्य धनमक्षय्यं त्वदीयं भरतर्षभ ।\nउदक्रोशन्महेष्वासा नरेन्द्र विजितारयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having got your inexhaustible wealth, O best of Bharatas, those great archers, conquerors of their enemies, shouted aloud, O king."}},{"n":34,"text":"ते तु वीराः समाश्वस्य वाहनान्यवमुच्य च ।\nअतिष्ठन्त मुहुः सर्वे पाण्डवाः सात्यकिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those heroes then took rest and unyoked their conveyances, and all the Pandavas and Satyaki stayed there for a while."}},{"n":35,"text":"अथाब्रवीन्महाराज वासुदेवो महायशाः ।\nअस्माभिर्मङ्गलार्थाय वस्तव्यं शिबिराद्बहिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the greatly renowned Vasudeva said, great king: \"For good fortune, we should stay outside the camp.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा च ते सर्वे पाण्डवाः सात्यकिस्तथा ।\nवासुदेवेन सहिता मङ्गलार्थं ययुर्बहिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" all the Pandavas and Satyaki went with Vasudeva outside the camp for good fortune."}},{"n":37,"text":"ते समासाद्य सरितं पुण्यामोघवतीं नृप ।\nन्यवसन्नथ तां रात्रिं पाण्डवा हतशत्रवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the holy river Oghavati, O king, the Pandavas, their enemies slain, spent that night there."}},{"n":38,"text":"ततः संप्रेषयामासुर्यादवं नागसाह्वयम् ।\nस च प्रायाज्जवेनाशु वासुदेवः प्रतापवान् ।\nदारुकं रथमारोप्य येन राजाम्बिकासुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they sent the Yadava to Hastinapura. Powerful Vasudeva quickly went at speed, placing Daruka in the chariot, to where the son of Ambika, the king, was."}},{"n":39,"text":"तमूचुः संप्रयास्यन्तं सैन्यसुग्रीववाहनम् ।\nप्रत्याश्वासय गान्धारीं हतपुत्रां यशस्विनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he was about to leave, with his chariot drawn by Sainya and Sugriva, they said to him: \"Comfort the renowned Gandhari, whose son is dead.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"स प्रायात्पाण्डवैरुक्तस्तत्पुरं सात्वतां वरः ।\nआससादयिषुः क्षिप्रं गान्धारीं निहतात्मजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so by the Pandavas, that best of the Satvatas went to that city, wishing to reach Gandhari, whose sons had been killed, quickly."}}]}]}